UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Chocolate Brownies are an American creation dating to the late 19th century, with the first known recipe appearing in the 1893 Sears, Roebuck catalog. The fudgy, dense chocolate square has become one of the world''s most beloved desserts, representing American baking at its most indulgent.' WHERE slug = 'chocolate-brownies';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Caesar Salad was created in 1924 by Italian-American restaurateur Caesar Cardini in Tijuana, Mexico. This iconic salad of romaine lettuce, croutons, and Parmesan with a creamy dressing has become one of the most popular salads in the world.' WHERE slug = 'caesar-salad-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Deviled Eggs have ancient Roman origins but became an American party staple in the 19th century. The term "deviled" refers to the spicy mustard seasoning. These stuffed egg halves are an essential appetizer at every American gathering from holidays to potlucks.' WHERE slug = 'deviled-eggs-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Flourless Chocolate Torte is a rich, dense chocolate cake popular in American fine dining. Its origins trace to European torte traditions, but the flourless version gained popularity in the 1980s-90s as both a gluten-free option and a decadent dessert showcasing pure chocolate flavor.' WHERE slug = 'flourless-torte-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Lavender Lemonade represents the modern American craft beverage movement, combining classic lemonade with culinary lavender. This refreshing drink reflects the farm-to-table trend and the growing American interest in herb-infused beverages.' WHERE slug = 'lavender-lemonade-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Massaged Kale Salad emerged from the 2010s superfood movement that elevated kale from a garnish to a dietary staple. The technique of massaging raw kale with oil and acid softens its tough leaves, making this nutrient-dense green accessible and delicious.' WHERE slug = 'kale-apple-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'No-Knead Artisan Bread revolutionized home baking when Jim Lahey''s recipe appeared in the New York Times in 2006. By using a long, slow fermentation and a Dutch oven, home bakers could achieve bakery-quality crusty bread without kneading. It democratized artisan bread-making.' WHERE slug = 'no-knead-artisan-bread-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Pigs in a Blanket are a beloved American party snack of mini hot dogs wrapped in crescent roll dough. While the concept exists in various forms across cultures, the American version became a cocktail party staple in the 1950s-60s and remains an essential party food.' WHERE slug = 'pigs-in-blanket-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Butternut Squash Soup is an American autumn comfort food that celebrates the winter squash harvest. Squash is native to the Americas, cultivated by Indigenous peoples for over 10,000 years. This creamy, warming soup represents the seasonal cooking traditions of American home kitchens.' WHERE slug = 'butternut-soup-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Shrimp Cocktail became an iconic American appetizer in the mid-20th century, symbolizing sophistication and celebration. Served in a martini glass with cocktail sauce, it became a steakhouse and party essential that represents the golden age of American entertaining.' WHERE slug = 'shrimp-cocktail-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Sourdough Discard Crackers emerged from the sourdough bread baking revival, especially during the 2020 pandemic. Rather than discarding excess starter, bakers transformed it into crispy crackers, embodying the zero-waste cooking philosophy.' WHERE slug = 'sourdough-crackers-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Stuffed Mushrooms are a classic American appetizer that became popular in the mid-20th century. Filled with cheese, herbs, and breadcrumbs, these bite-sized treats represent the American tradition of creative finger foods for entertaining.' WHERE slug = 'stuffed-mushrooms-us';

UPDATE recipes SET continent = 'North America', history = 'Sweet Potato Mash with Maple combines two indigenous American ingredients: sweet potatoes, cultivated for over 5,000 years, and maple syrup, harvested by Native Americans for centuries. This comforting side dish represents the deep roots of American food traditions.' WHERE slug = 'sweet-potato-mash-us';

